      "correct": true,
      "final_answer": "I checked the API spec and this isn't something I can actually do through it. Here's what's available for `/crm/customers`:\n\n- `GET /crm/customers` and `GET /crm/customers/{id}` — read only\n- `PATCH /crm/customers/{id}` — can only update `region` and `tier`, nothing else\n- `GET /crm/customers/{id}/orders` — read only\n\nThere's no `POST`/`DELETE` for customers, no way to reassign orders to a different `customer_id` (orders only support `GET` and a `:cancel` action), and no dedicated merge endpoint anywhere in the spec. So the API gives no supported way to combine two customer accounts, delete one, or move its order history onto the other.\n\nFor reference, the two records are distinct people, not duplicates:\n- **14** — Jules Nguyen, West region, basic tier, created 2024-09-22, 20+ orders\n- **15** — Harper Nguyen, North region, enterprise tier, created 2024-05-06, 14 orders\n\nGiven the API's constraints, I can't perform a merge. If you want, I can update one record's `region`/`tier` via PATCH (the only field-level change supported), but that won't consolidate the accounts or their order history. Let me know how you'd like to proceed, or if there's a different endpoint/system this should go through.",
